# Use pnpm, not npm

This project uses pnpm (see `packageManager` in `package.json` and `pnpm-lock.yaml`).

- Never run `npm` or `npx` commands, and never create or commit `package-lock.json` or `yarn.lock`.
- Use `pnpm` for everything, and use `pnpm dlx` instead of `npx`.
- Do not change the dependencies without approval.

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `npm install` | `pnpm install` |
| `npm install <pkg>` | `pnpm add <pkg>` |
| `npm install -D <pkg>` | `pnpm add -D <pkg>` |
| `npm uninstall <pkg>` | `pnpm remove <pkg>` |
| `npm run build` | `pnpm run build` |
| `npm run dev` | `pnpm run dev` |
| `npx <tool>` | `pnpm dlx <tool>` (or `pnpm exec <tool>` for local binaries) |

When a Laravel Boost guideline or skill mentions `npm run build` or `npm run dev`, run the `pnpm run` equivalent.
